# content/insights

Source-of-truth folder for /insights articles. Each .md / .mdx file becomes a
static page at /insights/<filename-without-extension>.

Required frontmatter (YAML between ---):

  title:         string
  summary:       string (1-2 sentences)
  datePublished: YYYY-MM-DD or ISO 8601 datetime
  dateModified:  YYYY-MM-DD (optional)
  authorSlug:    slug from src/data/instructors.ts, or omit for Organization
  image:         /path/to/og-or-hero.jpg (optional)
  tags:          [Six Sigma, DMAIC, ...]
  draft:         true to keep in repo but hide from /insights and sitemap
  citations:     [{ url, title }] — external sources you cite (Article.citation)
  mentions:      [{ url, name }] — on-site entities you reference (Article.mentions)

Body is regular Markdown. MDX (component embedding) is supported via the file
extension but requires extra wiring — start with plain .md.

Editorial pillars (Phase D.1 of the SEO plan):
  1. Six Sigma in SA industries (mining, automotive, banking, public sector)
  2. Comparison content (Six Sigma vs ISO 9001, Lean vs Agile in SA call centres)
  3. Original SA-specific data (State of Quality Management in SA — annual)
  4. Regulatory framing (MICT SETA, SAQA, B-BBEE skills-spend implications)
